DESCRIPTION:This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at
	 no extra cost to you. \nGet Tickets \nAbout the Show\nKick off the weeken
	d the right way at the iconic Comic Strip Live with “Thank Comedy It’s Fri
	day” — New York City’s premier late-night stand-up comedy show. Featuring 
	hilarious sets from top comedians seen on Netflix\, HBO\, Comedy Central\,
	 BET\, and viral social media platforms\, this is the perfect way to shake
	 off the week. \nDJ E.M. provides a live show soundtrack to keep the energ
	y high all night long. Bring your friends\, grab a drink\, and enjoy an ev
	ening packed with jokes\, good vibes\, and great company. \nEvent Details\
	nDate: August 7\, 2026Time: Doors open at 10:00 PM\; Showtime starts at 10
	:30 PMVenue: The Comic Strip (Comic Strip Live)Address: 1568 2nd Avenue\, 
	New York\, NY 10028City: New York\, NYPrice: $25.00 General AdmissionAge R
	estriction: 21+ with valid IDNote: Two-item minimum purchase per person re
	quired \nAbout the Venue\nThe Comic Strip is one of New York City’s most i
	conic comedy clubs\, located at 1568 2nd Avenue on the Upper East Side. A 
	legendary launching pad for countless comedy careers\, this intimate venue
	 has hosted some of the biggest names in stand-up. Accessible via the 77th
	 St (6 train) and 86th St (Q train) subway stations. \nWhat to Expect\nExp
	ect a high-energy late-night comedy experience with a rotating lineup of t
	op-tier talent from Netflix and Comedy Central. The live DJ soundtrack kee
	ps the atmosphere electric from the moment you walk in until the last punc
	hline lands. \nThis is the ultimate Friday night out in NYC — laughs\, dri
	nks\, and great vibes at one of the city’s most storied comedy venues. \nT
	icket Information\nTickets are available through Fever. General Admission 
	is $25.00. Must be 21+ with valid ID. A two-item minimum purchase per pers
	on is required at the event. \nGet Tickets\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/e
	vent/thank-comedy-its-friday-late-night-stand-up-show-live-at-the-comic-st
	rip-aug/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
