UID:mIgFi5Sut0_xcnzgxb_dg
SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live LIVE at Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall (Saturday Show)
DTSTAMP:20260808T093526Z
DTSTART:20260808T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nAli Wong 
	is an Emmy Award-winning actress\, comedian\, writer\, and producer who ha
	s become one of the most celebrated voices in stand-up comedy. Born and ra
	ised in San Francisco\, Ali broke through with her wildly popular Netflix 
	specials Baby Cobra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while 
	she was visibly pregnant — a bold and hilarious choice that became her sig
	nature. \nHer fourth Netflix special\, Ali Wong: Single Lady (2024)\, earn
	ed her a Golden Globe Award and a Critics Choice TV Award nomination. She 
	also starred in and executive produced the acclaimed Netflix/A24 dark come
	dy series Beef (2023)\, for which she won the Emmy\, Golden Globe\, Critic
	s Choice\, and Screen Actors Guild Awards for Best Actress in a Limited Se
	ries. \nAli’s comedy is raw\, confessional\, and unapologetically honest —
	 covering topics from relationships and family life to identity and ambiti
	on with a fearless comedic voice that resonates deeply with audiences worl
	dwide. \nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, August 8\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM (
	Doors open 1 hour before showtime) \nVenue: Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall 
	— 1037 SW Broadway Ave\, Portland\, OR 97205 \nTicket Limit: 6 tickets per
	 household \nNote: This is Show 2 of 2 Portland performances. A first show
	 takes place on August 7\, 2026. This second show was added due to popular
	 demand! \nAbout the Venue\nThe Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall — lovingly c
	alled “The Schnitz” by Portlanders — is one of the Pacific Northwest’s mos
	t treasured performance spaces. Situated in the heart of downtown Portland
	 at 1037 SW Broadway Ave\, this magnificent 2\,776-seat venue is part of t
	he Portland’5 Centers for the Arts complex. \nOriginally constructed in 19
	28 as the Portland Public Theatre\, the hall was meticulously restored and
	 reopened in 1984. Its stunning Italian Baroque architecture\, ornate inte
	rior details\, and world-class acoustics create an unforgettable atmospher
	e for live performances. Every seat in the house offers excellent sightlin
	es to the stage. \nThe venue features orchestra\, mezzanine\, and balcony 
	seating levels\, along with a full bar\, concessions\, and accessible seat
	ing options. Parking is available in nearby downtown Portland garages\, an
	d the venue is conveniently accessible via TriMet public transit. Phone: 5
	03-248-4335. \nWhat to Expect\nAli Wong Live is a full evening of stand-up
	 comedy featuring Ali’s signature confessional and boundary-pushing humor.
	 Based on recent tour reviews\, the show runs approximately 60–75 minutes 
	including an opening act. \nExpect Ali at her most personal and hilarious 
	— sharing stories from her life post-divorce\, her experiences as a workin
	g mother\, and her unique perspective on modern relationships and identity
	. Her comedy is sharp\, relatable\, and delivered with incredible energy a
	nd timing. \nThe Saturday show was added due to overwhelming demand for th
	e Friday performance — a testament to Ali Wong’s massive popularity with P
	ortland audiences. The Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall provides an intimate 
	and elegant setting\, with exceptional acoustics and a warm atmosphere tha
	t makes every seat feel close to the action. \nTicket Information\nPrice R
	ange: From $120 (resale prices may vary) \nThis second Portland show was a
	dded due to popular demand — don’t miss your chance to see Ali Wong live! 
	\nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We 
	may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.c
	om/event/ali-wong-live-at-arlene-schnitzer-concert-hall-saturday/\n\nFrom 
	Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-at-arlene-schnitzer-conc
	ert-hall-saturday/
LOCATION:Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall\, 1037 SW Broadway Ave\, Portland\, 
	Oregon\, 97205\, United States Of America
